  "conclusions": ["No engine-error, rejected-action, unresolved-settlement, or unexpected fallback-power cases in the recorded before/after runs. Startup shuffles are counted separately; zero fallback power does not mean zero startup reshuffling.","Fixed-sample objective authored completion increased from 143/160 to 156/160. Fresh holdout completion increased from 333/370 to 352/370; remaining work also decreased.","The independent holdout retains a level-28 difficulty candidate: 5/10 completed with mean target coverage 97.59%; failures mostly leave one or two gifts with two to five hits, sometimes four jelly cells. This is not a claim that every sharp or subjective difficulty issue is solved.","First-hint completion fell slightly in two early bands despite better mean goal coverage. Results are policy-dependent; no claim of universal completion-rate improvement is made.","A strong visible-board policy clears nearly all sampled generated levels. Its outcome and move slack are not human win-rate measurements or evidence of original-game difficulty equivalence.","The holdout seeds were requested only after gameplay source was frozen and were not used in the earlier tuning runs. Any subsequent tuning against these results would require a new independent holdout."],
